data: {"type": "assistant_msg", "ts": "2026-08-06T12:19:06.731699+00:00", "content": "I've retrieved the SD-WAN tunnel latency metrics for **ce_branch24** over the last ~24 hours. The data covers 6 tunnels (to ce_hub1 through ce_hub6) with samples roughly every 45-60 minutes. Here's the evidence and a summary you can use for plotting:\n\n## Raw Data Points (all from `query_metrics` with `pattern=\"latency\"`, `ranged=true`)\n\n| Tunnel | Sample Count | Latency Range (ms) | Avg (ms) | Key Evidence IDs |\n|--------|--------------|-------------------|----------|------------------|\n| **ce_branch24 \u2192 ce_hub1** | 20 | 67.4 \u2013 106.1 | ~82.3 | [metrics:0]\u2013[metrics:18] |\n| **ce_branch24 \u2192 ce_hub2** | 19 | 61.2 \u2013 97.0 | ~73.1 | [metrics:19]\u2013[metrics:37] |\n| **ce_branch24 \u2192 ce_hub3** | 19 | 68.9 \u2013 111.7 | ~85.2 | [metrics:38]\u2013[metrics:56] |\n| **ce_branch24 \u2192 ce_hub4** | 19 | 65.8 \u2013 102.8 | ~81.4 | [metrics:57]\u2013[metrics:75] |\n| **ce_branch24 \u2192 ce_hub5** | 19 | 60.8 \u2013 100.2 | ~76.8 | [metrics:76]\u2013[metrics:94] |\n| **ce_branch24 \u2192 ce_hub6** | 4 (partial) | 69.6 \u2013 119.7 | ~93.8 | [metrics:95]\u2013[metrics:98] |\n\n## Notable Patterns\n- **Periodic spikes** every ~4\u20135 hours on most tunnels (e.g., ~105\u2013111 ms at ts\u22481785950220, 1785981690, 1785977190), suggesting a recurring load or routing change.\n- **ce_hub3** and **ce_hub6** consistently show the highest peaks (up to 111\u2013119 ms).\n- **ce_hub2** and **ce_hub5** are the most stable (lowest averages, tightest ranges).\n- All tunnels show a **baseline of 60\u201375 ms** with **excursions to 90\u2013110 ms**.\n\n## Time Range\n- First sample: `ts=1785936750` (\u2248 2024-08-05 00:12 UTC)\n- Last sample:  `ts=1786018650` (\u2248 2024-08-05 23:17 UTC)\n- **Coverage: ~23 hours**, matching your 24-hour window.\n\n## Next Steps for Plotting\nSince I cannot render charts, you can:\n1. **Export the above points** (each row: `timestamp, tunnel, latency_ms`) into CSV/JSON.\n2. Plot **time-series lines per tunnel** (6 series) in Grafana, Excel, Python (matplotlib/plotly), etc.\n3. Overlay a **rolling average** or **max envelope** to highlight the periodic spikes.\n\nWould you like me to fetch the next page (`offset=100`) to complete the ce_hub6 series, or pull jitter/loss metrics for the same tunnels to correlate?"}

